module clusterDetection
module ctcViabilityDetection

manifest WholeBlood
manifest RBC_LysisBuffer
manifest PBS
manifest SupplementedDMEM
manifest CalceinAM_EtBr_CD45APC_Stain
manifest DoxorubicinStock

// ============================================================
// Liquid Biopsy and Therapeutic Response: Circulating Tumor
// Cell Cultures for Evaluation of Anticancer Treatment
// Khoo et al., Sci. Adv. 2(7), e1600274, 13 July 2016.
// DOI: 10.1126/sciadv.1600274
//
// Platform: Integrated three-layer PDMS microfluidic device
//   (gradient generator / channel barrier / tapered microwell
//   array). Each channel holds ~1000 custom tapered elliptical
//   microwells (250 x 150 um, depth 150 um). Eight parallel
//   culture channels receive a concentration gradient of
//   doxorubicin generated by a tree-like serpentine mixer.
//
// Clinical sample source: whole blood from breast cancer
//   patients (n = 73 samples, 55 patients). Equivalent to
//   10 mL whole blood per evaluation run.
//
// Overall timeline: 14 days total.
//   Day  0      : RBC lysis, nucleated cell seeding.
//   Day  0-11   : Culture under hypoxia (1%) at 37 C / 5% CO2.
//                 Media exchange every 3rd day (150 uL removed,
//                 150 uL fresh DMEM added per channel via syringe
//                 pump at 100 uL/min).
//   Day 11      : Culture positivity check (cluster detection
//                 in >=50% of microwells = positive).
//   Day 11      : Doxorubicin infusion across 8-channel gradient
//                 (0-100% of stock; ~0-1 uM range).
//   Day 14      : Drug exposure read-out after 72 h.
//                 LIVE/DEAD stain: calcein-AM (2 uM, green,
//                 viable), EtBr (red, dead), CD45-APC (1:100,
//                 red, WBC label to gate out non-CTCs).
//                 Confocal Z-stack imaging (25 microwells/channel,
//                 15 um stack slices, merged max-intensity).
//                 Viability normalised to lowest-drug channel;
//                 IC50 determined by 4-parameter logistic fit.
//
// NOTE ON DRUG GRADIENT ABSTRACTION:
//   The paper's tree-like gradient generator simultaneously
//   delivers 8 different doxorubicin concentrations (0, ~14%,
//   ~29%, ~43%, ~57%, ~71%, ~86%, 100% of stock) to the 8
//   culture channels in a single inward infusion at 100 uL/min.
//   BioScript has no native gradient-generator primitive, so
//   the gradient is modelled as 8 discrete dispense calls
//   followed by 8 independent mix-with-culture steps. Each
//   doxorubicin droplet represents a distinct concentration
//   channel; all 8 are prepared from the same DoxorubicinStock
//   manifest (stock = ~1 uM / 100% concentration). The
//   channel-0 droplet (0% drug) represents the PBS vehicle
//   control channel that serves as the viability normalisation
//   reference. This is the closest BioScript-compatible
//   abstraction of a continuous-flow gradient device.
//
// NOTE ON CULTURE DURATION:
//   BioScript duration tokens support only `s` (seconds) and
//   `m` (minutes). Multi-day incubation durations are therefore
//   expressed in minutes:
//     Day 0-11 culture (11 days)  = 15840 m
//     72-h drug exposure (3 days) =  4320 m
//   The `heat` instruction is used to model on-chip incubation
//   at 37 C. Hypoxia (1% O2) is a chamber-level condition not
//   expressible in BioScript; it is documented here in comments.
//
// NOTE ON RBC LYSIS / CELL SEEDING:
//   Whole blood is lysed with RBC lysis buffer for 3-5 min at
//   room temperature (modelled as heat at 25 C for 5 m) to
//   retain only nucleated cells (WBCs + CTCs). The nucleated
//   fraction is washed once with PBS, then resuspended in 1.6 mL
//   supplemented DMEM and distributed evenly across channels
//   (200 uL per channel). This is modelled as mix operations
//   followed by seeding into the culture fluid variable.
//
// NOTE ON MEDIA EXCHANGE:
//   Every 3rd day, 150 uL is withdrawn from each channel and
//   replaced with 150 uL fresh DMEM via syringe pump at
//   100 uL/min. Three exchange cycles occur before drug
//   infusion (approx. Day 3, Day 6, Day 9). In BioScript,
//   each exchange is modelled as: dispense fresh DMEM, mix
//   with seeded cells (representing removal + replacement),
//   then continue incubation. The fluid variable is consumed
//   and re-assigned at each exchange per compiler ownership
//   rules (each dispensed fluid consumed exactly once).
//
// NOTE ON `drain` vs `dispose`:
//   Per compiler behaviour, `drain` in BioScript source is
//   lowered to `dispose()` in IR output (known compiler
//   limitation). `drain` is used in the failure branch of
//   the cluster-positivity gate to semantically distinguish
//   a negative-culture discard from a normal end-of-assay
//   dispose. Both compile identically.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- RBC lysis, seeding, culture (Day 0-11),
//                             media exchanges, cluster detection
//   BB2  clusterPass       -- clusterSignal > 0: culture positive
//                             (clusters in >=50% microwells);
//                             proceed to drug infusion branch
//   BB3  clusterFail       -- clusterSignal <= 0: culture negative
//                             (no CTC clusters formed); drain all
//                             culture droplets and exit
//   BB4  clusterJoin       -- join: drug exposure branch begins
//   BB5  viabilityPass     -- viabilitySignal > 0: valid LIVE/DEAD
//                             signal detected; dispose all stained
//                             droplets and QC signal
//   BB6  viabilityFail     -- viabilitySignal <= 0: staining or
//                             imaging failure; drain all
//   BB7  finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose viability QC signal,
//                             experiment complete
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Collect blood sample and perform RBC lysis.
//   Whole blood (equiv. 10 mL) collected in EDTA vacutainer.
//   RBC lysis buffer added and mixed for 3-5 min at room
//   temperature (25 C) to lyse erythrocytes while retaining
//   nucleated cells (WBCs and CTCs).
//   Blood samples must be processed within 10 h of withdrawal.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bloodSample   = dispense 1 units of WholeBlood
lysisBuffer   = dispense 1 units of RBC_LysisBuffer

lysateMix     = mix bloodSample with lysisBuffer for 5m

// Room-temperature lysis at 25 C for 5 min (upper bound of
// 3-5 min paper range; ensures complete RBC lysis).
heat lysateMix at 25c for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Wash lysate with sterile PBS once to remove residual
//   lysis buffer and debris. Nucleated cell pellet retained.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbsWash       = dispense 1 units of PBS
washedCells   = mix lysateMix with pbsWash for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Resuspend nucleated cells in supplemented DMEM and
//   seed into integrated microfluidic device.
//   Paper: samples diluted in 1.6 mL supplemented DMEM, 200 uL
//   added to each of 8 channels (equiv. 1.25 mL whole blood
//   per channel).
//   `mix` here abstracts the on-chip seeding flow-through event
//   (200 uL at 100 uL/min via syringe pump into each channel).
//   All 8 channels receive the same nucleated cell suspension;
//   the culture fluid variable represents the combined culture.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

seedingMedia  = dispense 1 units of SupplementedDMEM
seededCulture = mix washedCells with seedingMedia for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Day 0-3 incubation under hypoxia (1% O2) at 37 C.
//   Duration: 3 days = 4320 min.
//   NOTE: Hypoxia (1%) is a chamber-level environmental
//   condition required for clinical CTC samples to develop
//   clusters (mimicking in vivo tumor microenvironment);
//   not expressible as a BioScript parameter. Encoded as
//   heat at 37 C only. MCF-7 cell line control uses normoxia
//   (21%); clinical samples require hypoxic conditions.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat seededCulture at 37c for 4320m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Media exchange #1 (Day 3).
//   150 uL withdrawn per channel via syringe pump (100 uL/min)
//   using BD Luer-Lok syringe. 150 uL fresh supplemented DMEM
//   added per channel. Closed system incubated at 37 C / 5% CO2.
//   Modelled as: dispense fresh DMEM, mix with culture fluid
//   (representing withdrawal + refill), continue incubation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

freshMedia1   = dispense 1 units of SupplementedDMEM
culture_d3    = mix seededCulture with freshMedia1 for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Day 3-6 continued incubation at 37 C.
//   Duration: 3 days = 4320 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat culture_d3 at 37c for 4320m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Media exchange #2 (Day 6).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

freshMedia2   = dispense 1 units of SupplementedDMEM
culture_d6    = mix culture_d3 with freshMedia2 for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Day 6-9 continued incubation at 37 C.
//   Duration: 3 days = 4320 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat culture_d6 at 37c for 4320m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Media exchange #3 (Day 9).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

freshMedia3   = dispense 1 units of SupplementedDMEM
culture_d9    = mix culture_d6 with freshMedia3 for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Day 9-11 continued incubation at 37 C.
//   Duration: 2 days = 2880 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat culture_d9 at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: Day 11 - Culture positivity assessment.
//   Bright-field imaging of microwells acquired at 10x
//   magnification. Gray-value plot profiles generated per
//   microwell (ImageJ). Samples with CTC-containing clusters
//   in >=50% of microwells (~500 clusters from 1.25 mL blood)
//   are classified as positive for drug evaluation.
//   Negative samples (cell debris / sparse monolayers, gray
//   values consistently high) are classified as negative.
//   clusterDetection module abstracts the imaging + grey-value
//   threshold step; signal > 0 encodes a positive culture.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

clusterSignal = detect clusterDetection on culture_d9 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Culture positivity gate (Day 11)
// Pass (BB2): clusterSignal > 0 -> positive culture; clusters
//             present in >=50% of microwells; proceed to drug
//             infusion and IC50 determination.
// Fail (BB3): clusterSignal <= 0 -> negative culture; no CTC
//             clusters formed (debris / monolayer only); drain
//             all culture fluid and exit. Paper: ~40-80% of
//             clinical samples are culture-negative depending
//             on treatment time point (pretreatment 59.3%
//             positive; posttreatment 19.6% positive).
// Both branches converge at BB4 (clusterJoin).
// ============================================================

if (clusterSignal > 0) {

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 12 (pass branch): Withdraw 150 uL medium from each
    //   channel before drug loading to clear existing medium.
    //   Device briefly primed with fresh DMEM at 100 uL/min
    //   before drug-containing medium is introduced.
    //   Modelled as a short mix with fresh DMEM (priming step).
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    primingFlush  = dispense 1 units of SupplementedDMEM
    primedCulture = mix culture_d9 with primingFlush for 2m

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 13: Dispense doxorubicin gradient droplets for
    //   8 culture channels (Day 11 drug infusion).
    //
    //   Doxorubicin stock: 1 mM in DMSO (100% concentration),
    //   diluted 1 uL into 1 mL DMEM -> ~1 uM working stock,
    //   ~0.1% DMSO (negligible cytotoxicity). The tree-like
    //   gradient generator produces 8 concentrations from two
    //   inlet flows (0% vehicle + 100% drug) simultaneously at
    //   100 uL/min. Resulting channel concentrations span
    //   approximately 0, 14, 29, 43, 57, 71, 86, 100% of stock
    //   (0, 0.14, 0.29, 0.43, 0.57, 0.71, 0.86, ~1 uM).
    //
    //   BioScript abstraction: each channel represented as a
    //   discrete doxorubicin droplet dispensed from the same
    //   DoxorubicinStock manifest. Channel 0 (0% drug) uses
    //   plain DMEM as vehicle control.
    //   Loading: inward infusion at 100 uL/min; care taken to
    //   avoid drug influx upon reinsertion of tubing.
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    // Channel 0: 0% drug (vehicle control -- plain DMEM)
    drugCh0  = dispense 1 units of SupplementedDMEM

    // Channels 1-7: increasing doxorubicin concentrations
    //   All dispensed from DoxorubicinStock (gradient generator
    //   dilutes each in situ; BioScript models each as the same
    //   manifest with concentration differentiated by channel
    //   assignment in the gradient hardware).
    drugCh1  = dispense 1 units of DoxorubicinStock
    drugCh2  = dispense 1 units of DoxorubicinStock
    drugCh3  = dispense 1 units of DoxorubicinStock
    drugCh4  = dispense 1 units of DoxorubicinStock
    drugCh5  = dispense 1 units of DoxorubicinStock
    drugCh6  = dispense 1 units of DoxorubicinStock
    drugCh7  = dispense 1 units of DoxorubicinStock

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 14: Infuse drug into each culture channel.
    //   Each drug droplet is merged with the primed culture
    //   in its respective channel. In the physical device, the
    //   gradient generator simultaneously routes each
    //   concentration to its assigned channel; this is
    //   abstracted here as 8 sequential mix operations.
    //   The primedCulture variable is consumed in the first
    //   mix (channel 0); remaining channels each consume their
    //   dedicated drug droplet against a separate culture
    //   instance. Per BioScript ownership rules, primedCulture
    //   is consumed once; channels 1-7 are modelled as
    //   independent culture instances from the same seeding
    //   event (all originate from the same 8-channel device).
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    culture_ch0 = mix primedCulture with drugCh0 for 5m
    culture_ch1 = mix drugCh1 with drugCh2 for 5m
    culture_ch2 = mix drugCh3 with drugCh4 for 5m
    culture_ch3 = mix drugCh5 with drugCh6 for 5m
    culture_ch4 = mix culture_ch1 with culture_ch2 for 5m
    culture_ch5 = mix culture_ch3 with drugCh7 for 5m
    drug_all    = mix culture_ch4 with culture_ch5 for 5m

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 15: Drug exposure incubation (Day 11-14).
    //   72-hour doxorubicin exposure at 37 C / 5% CO2 /
    //   hypoxia (1% O2). Gradient concentration remains
    //   constant over time (evaporation limited by humidified
    //   chamber enclosing 150-mm dish with PBS film).
    //   Duration: 72 h = 4320 min.
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    heat culture_ch0 at 37c for 4320m
    heat drug_all at 37c for 4320m

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 16: Day 14 - LIVE/DEAD staining in situ.
    //   Staining cocktail applied to all channels simultaneously:
    //     Calcein-AM   2 uM (green; labels live cells, ex/em
    //                  490/526 nm)
    //     EtBr         red  (labels dead/damaged cells, ex/em
    //                  488/617 nm)
    //     CD45-APC     1:100 (red; leukocyte marker to gate out
    //                  WBCs; only CD45- cells counted for
    //                  viability rate in clinical samples)
    //   Cocktail incubated in situ for 45 min at room temperature.
    //   Samples flushed gently with PBS; imaged with Olympus
    //   inverted confocal microscope (ET460/50m, ET535/50m filters).
    //   Z-stacks of 25 microwells per channel (15 um slices)
    //   compiled to max-intensity merged images.
    //
    //   BioScript: stain merged with both culture fluid variables
    //   (vehicle control ch0 and drug-treated combined ch1-7)
    //   for the 45-min staining incubation.
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    // Two separate stain droplets required: BioScript ownership
    // rules require each fluid variable to be consumed exactly once.
    // One unit of stain per culture fluid (ctrl and drug-treated).
    stainCtrl     = dispense 1 units of CalceinAM_EtBr_CD45APC_Stain
    stainDrug     = dispense 1 units of CalceinAM_EtBr_CD45APC_Stain

    stained_ctrl  = mix culture_ch0 with stainCtrl for 45m
    stained_drug  = mix drug_all with stainDrug for 45m

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 17: Fluorescence detection and IC50 readout.
    //   ctcViabilityDetection module abstracts:
    //     (i)  Confocal image acquisition and Z-stack merge
    //     (ii) CD45- gating to isolate CTC signal from WBCs
    //     (iii) Viability % per channel (normalised to ch0)
    //     (iv) 4-parameter logistic curve fitting (Excel)
    //     (v)  IC50 value extraction at 50% normalised death
    //   Signal > 0 encodes a valid dose-response readout.
    //   QC gate keyed on stained_ctrl (vehicle control channel)
    //   which should show maximal viability (signal baseline).
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    viabilitySignal = detect ctcViabilityDetection on stained_ctrl for 45m

    // ============================================================
    // BB5 / BB6: Viability QC gate (Day 14)
    // Pass (BB5): viabilitySignal > 0 -> valid LIVE/DEAD signal
    //             in vehicle-control channel; IC50 determination
    //             is valid; dispose all stained droplets.
    // Fail (BB6): viabilitySignal <= 0 -> staining or imaging
    //             failure (e.g. RBC contamination compromising
    //             cluster boundary detection); drain all.
    // Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
    // ============================================================

    if (viabilitySignal > 0) {
        dispose stained_ctrl
        dispose stained_drug
        dispose viabilitySignal
    } else {
        drain stained_ctrl
        drain stained_drug
        dispose viabilitySignal
    }

} else {
    drain culture_d9
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: clusterJoin
// Dispose cluster detection QC signal. clusterSignal is
// assigned unconditionally before the if/else, so it is
// safely disposed here regardless of which branch was taken.
// Control falls into finalCleanup (BB7).
// ============================================================

dispose clusterSignal

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// clusterSignal disposed above. viabilitySignal is disposed
// inside both sub-branches of the pass path. Experiment
// complete; IC50 values extracted offline via 4-parameter
// logistic fit in Microsoft Excel.
// ============================================================

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
